      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "The complete author Theorem1.1 route is supplied: weighted Gauss Proposition4.2 with all local arithmetic proofs, Euler-Maclaurin Lemma5.2/Proposition5.3, the surgery formula6.1 and completion identities6.2–6.5. Select the negative-definite determinant-one six-vertex H linking matrix with all weights negative and leaf weights w3–w6<=-2, at integer levels k>=3 so the displayed normalization denominator is nonzero. These explicit restrictions exclude the separately known Seifert/degenerate-normalization edge cases. The exact principal-value homological block and standard S3-normalized WRT convention are retained. Existing surgery formula(6.1), Gauss reciprocity and two-variable Euler-Maclaurin are background; the author proves the new weighted cancellations and lattice completion. The general standalone auxiliary statements4.2/4.4 are not counted; their actual application is only on the nonzero support of the plumbing weight epsilon. Later quantum modularity is a consequence of a prior theorem and is not selected."
      },
